<p>Police and rescue officials said a suicide car bomb followed by gunfire hit the Fateh Khel police post in Bannu district, Khyber Pakhtunkhwa, late Saturday. Dawn and The Express Tribune, citing police and rescue officials, reported at least 15 police personnel were killed and three injured. AP-based reports put the death toll at 14, while Reuters-based reports said 12 officers were dead. Police said attackers rammed an explosives-laden vehicle into the checkpoint, then opened fire from multiple directions; Reuters-based accounts also said attackers ambushed officers sent to help. Rescue teams pulled three officers alive from the debris, while local hospitals declared an emergency. A militant alliance known as Ittehad-ul-Mujahideen claimed responsibility, Reuters-based reports said, while AP described the group claiming responsibility as a self-proclaimed breakaway faction of the Pakistan Taliban. Pakistani sources said security forces cordoned off the area after the attack and launched clearance or search operations.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/043_q_pmMHeHXSOu9AJ1UFXviQr7SMJwR7nqFicLTwCIkN7KhjJwJVcGgMzWGYOwumHfZBcH3xp1OwesaJhQYn7If2BThLTAbSdBjvdLzWM932pwtLoWpP-u2jUGirIRPT22cJRZjZfUQtMbFtS4VM1jsV936-SyMzVL1qzSbkj0CahXD4DlS76Ky9me53zh-Q88lVlD' alt='Pakistan&#x27;da düzenlenen intihar saldırısında 12 polis hayatını kaybetti' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Personnel present: Dawn said 18 police personnel were at the post when the attack began.</li><li>Communications: Sources said contact with the Fateh Khel post was briefly disrupted after the attack.</li><li>Structural damage: The blast destroyed the post, wrecked an armored vehicle stationed there and severely damaged nearby structures, according to Dawn and Turkish reports citing Pakistani media.</li><li>Citywide policing: After the attack, police intensified checkpoints and spot checks across Bannu.</li></ul><blockquote>Terrorists will never succeed in their evil intentions, - DIG Bannu Sajjad Khan</blockquote><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Bannu regional police: RPO Sajjad Khan led the police response, and police officials said Bannu personnel responded with bravery, courage and professional skill during the operation. (<a href='https://www.dawn.com/news/1999014/police-checkpost-attacked-in-bannu'>Dawn</a>)</li><li>Afghanistan’s Taliban authorities: The Taliban administration has denied Islamabad’s accusation that militants plan attacks from Afghan territory and has said armed violence inside Pakistan is Pakistan’s internal problem. (<a href='https://www.annahar.com/international/asia/308452/باكستان-مقتل-12-شرطيا-بانفجار-سيارة-وإطلاق-نار'>Annahar</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.al-monitor.com/originals/2026/05/twelve-pakistani-policemen-killed-car-bombing'>Twelve Pakistani policemen killed in car bombing</a> - al-monitor.com</li><li><a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/twelve-pakistani-police-officers-killed-in-car-bombing-and-shootout/article70961523.ece'>Twelve Pakistani police officers killed in car bombing and shootout</a> - thehindu.com</li><li><a href='https://abcnews.com/International/wireStory/death-toll-rises-14-pakistan-suicide-attack-pakistan-132822359'>Death toll rises to 14 in Pakistan suicide attack. Taliban splinter group claim blast</a> - abcnews.com</li><li><a href='https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/5/9/three-police-officers-killed-in-car-bomb-attack-in-northwest-pakistan'>Car bomb attack and ambush in northwest Pakistan kills at least 12 police</a> - aljazeera.com</li><li><a href='https://www.dw.com/en/pakistan-car-bomb-attack-at-checkpoint-kills-12/a-77108185'>Pakistan: Car bomb attack at checkpoint kills 12</a> - dw.com</li><li><a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/middle-east/three-pakistani-police-officers-killed-in-car-bombing-more-casualties-feared'>Twelve Pakistani police officers killed in car bombing, shoot-out</a> - straitstimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.timesofisrael.com